# Milestone: M3
# Covers: System.memCheck() verifies no memory leak for repeated allocation
#         patterns: job creation (',', '&'), Object.new(), Tag.new(), parser,
#         string conversion, Lobby creation.
# defer-to: M6 (requires System.memCheck(), System.status(), System.Platform, and M6 stdlib types)
#
# Reason:
#   System.memCheck() is a test-harness helper that measures VmData growth across
#   an iteration loop.  It requires System.status() (M4 stdlib), System.Platform
#   (M4 stdlib), Lobby.create() (M4), ',' and '&' separator runtime (M5 chk
#   driver), Tag.new() method (M4), and Lobby.quit() (M4).  This is a full-stack
#   memory regression test — appropriate to activate after M6 when the stdlib is
#   feature-complete.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6+ with full System stdlib):
# # import System.*;
# # function init_memCheck() { ... }|;
# # init_memCheck();
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/mem-check.chk)
